# BACK SQUAT

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Back Squat is a bilateral lower-body compound exercise designed to develop force production through coordinated extension of the hips, knees and ankles.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for developing lower-body strength and power.

---

# Philosophy

The Back Squat is not simply a leg exercise.

It is a whole-body movement requiring coordinated force production, trunk stability and efficient movement mechanics.

CAS selects the Back Squat when maximal lower-body force production provides meaningful transfer to the athlete's performance goals.

